    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nThere appears to be a serious regression in terminal input performance on Windows.\nSending a sufficiently long string to a terminal is extremely slow, taking several seconds and making terminal interaction effectively unusable.\nThe slowdown is strongly dependent on the length of the string (I suspect some N^2 algorithm on characters is involved?!). The longer the string, more severe is the lag.\nThis do not happens on my linux machine, only on Windows. Latest binary, and mingw ucrt64 package, with different terminal emulators.\n\n## Latest nvim binary\n\n```text\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1286+g2450ae797c\nBuild type: RelWithDebInfo\n```\n\n* OS: Windows_NT 10.0.26100\n* Terminal: Alacritty\n\n## Latest mingw package\n\n```text\nNVIM v0.12.4\nBuild type: Release\nLuaJIT 2.1.1785606157\n```\n\n* OS: MINGW32_NT-10.0 10.0.26100\n* Terminal: mintty 3.8.3\n* Package: `mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-neovim 0.12.4-1`\n\nI reproduce the issue with both environments.\nOn older versions of nvim I didn't have this problem... I don't know tho what update introduced it.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```text\nnvim --clean\n```\n\nOpen a terminal using a bash shell. \nSending a short string is instantaneous:\n\n```vim\n:lua vim.api.nvim_chan_send(vim.b.terminal_job_id, \"echo \" .. string.rep(\"a\", 10))\n```\nSending a longer string is noticeably slow:\n\n```vim\n:lua vim.api.nvim_chan_send(vim.b.terminal_job_id, \"echo \" .. string.rep(\"a\", 100))\n```\n\nSending an even longer string is significantly slower:\n\n```vim\n:lua vim.api.nvim_chan_send(vim.b.terminal_job_id, \"echo \" .. string.rep(\"a\", 300))\n```\n\nThe slowdown increases with the length of the string.\nThe same behavior occurs when injecting the text through other Neovim APIs, including:\n\n```lua\nvim.api.nvim_command([[call feedkeys(\"Gi]] .. cmd_args)\n```\n\nand:\n\n```lua\nvim.api.nvim_paste(cmd_args, false, -1)\n```\n\nFor comparison, manually typing the same text into the terminal does **not** exhibit the slowdown.\n\nAlso, terminal output itself does not appear to be generally affected. For example, starting a process that immediately produces a long string is instantaneous:\n\n```vim\n:lua vim.fn.termopen({\"printf\", string.rep(\"a\", 300)})\n```\n\nThe problem appears to specifically affect programmatically sending/injecting longer strings into an existing terminal.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nSending a few hundred characters to a terminal should be effectively instantaneous, regardless of whether the text is entered manually or programmatically.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev-1286+g2450ae797c\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nIt is faster and lag do not scale with lenght\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nWindows 11\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nmintty, alacritty\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256-color\n\n### Installation\n\nrelease binary, mingw ucrt64 package",
